{%- comment -%}
MessagePack, on every generated contract. See the named template beside this for why overriding
Class.Annotations is enough to add an attribute and change nothing else.

Keyed mode, and the condition is load-bearing. A keyed object needs an index for every member, and
the document carries x-message-pack-index only on the schemas the contract keyed - the framework's
own error envelopes, ErrorModel and RequestValidationError, are in the same document and carry
none. Marking those [MessagePackObject] would not compile, so they take the named form with the
wire name pinned, which is exactly what the server writes them as.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign unkeyed = 0 -%}
{%- for property in Properties -%}
{%-   if property.ExtensionData == nil or property.ExtensionData["x-message-pack-index"] == nil -%}
{%-     assign unkeyed = unkeyed | plus: 1 -%}
{%-   endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if unkeyed == 0 and Properties.size > 0 -%}
[MessagePack.MessagePackObject]
{%- else -%}
[MessagePack.MessagePackObject(true)]
{%- endif -%}
